  "notes": [
    "Each figure is a single run of TestGuestWorkloadBenchmark on a shared laptop VM, with no baseline.",
    "The machine is the benchmark's: 2 GiB RAM, 8 GiB PMEM root, 4 vCPUs, a 3 GiB resident budget, 1 MiB flush batches and a 1 MiB read-ahead window in every run; flush_pages and read_ahead_pages are those sizes in the run's pages.",
    "The fork fan-out ran git grep rather than the default cargo test, which alone would take far longer than the five-minute budget of one run. Its only output is its result, so its first output is its completion, which is why every run failed the harness's two-second first-output bound; nothing else failed.",
    "pnpm-install is guest wall time from the guest's own accounting. Log bytes are the bytes region flushes wrote to the volumes during pnpm-install (Stats.FlushWriteBytes), and log bytes per flush divides them by the region flushes the volumes acknowledged (Stats.Flushes).",
    "Fork memory is what each fork's regions hold once its command finished (Region.Stats), summed over ram0 and root: resident is pages holding host memory, private is pages whose bytes are the fork's own. Means are over the four forks, in bytes.",
    "Boot phases: vmm_start is vmmachine.Start, kernel and init are the guest's monotonic clock, pre_kernel is the remainder of the wall time to readiness."
